# hub.tsl — both hub legs, aggregator's firehose ingest and hub-control's
# settings/discovery egress, in one worker. Frontmatter is read from the
# top-level file only, so both `var` pins below must live here — an included
# file's own frontmatter is skipped.
#
# `num_partitions = 1` does two things at once: it keeps hub-control's
# single-instance control plane single (without it, a hub configured above
# one data partition would mount that plane once per partition), and it means
# every Remote_Source child the firehose group builds pulls the spoke's
# `firehose.p0` alone. A spoke running more than one partition needs
# `aggregator` and `hub-control` activated as their own topology instead,
# with `num_partitions` matching the spoke's count.
#
# `on_demand_idle = 0` keeps the worker from idling out between ticks, so the
# hub's SSE pulls and its outbound settings/discovery commands stay open
# rather than cold-starting on the next reconcile pass.

var on_demand_idle = 0
var num_partitions = 1
include aggregator
include hub-control
secure
